# Age-Structured Network SIR Model for Disease Transmission Analysis

## Overview

This project implements an age-structured discrete-time SIR (Susceptible-Infected-Recovered) epidemic model on contact networks. It analyzes disease transmission dynamics across different countries with varying demographic structures, focusing on age-specific infection patterns and network properties.

## Key Features

- **Age-Structured Modeling**: 16 age groups (0-75+ years) with realistic population distributions
- **Network-Based Simulation**: Contact networks constructed from country-specific demographic data
- **Multi-Country Comparison**: Analysis of Germany, Uganda, Qatar, and Monaco
- **Intervention Scenarios**: Baseline, no-school, and no-work intervention models
- **Comprehensive Visualization**: Chord diagrams, heatmaps, time series, and statistical comparisons

## Project Structure

### Core Scripts

- `network_contruct.py` - Constructs contact networks from population and contact matrix data
- `age_structured_discrete_SIR_model.py` - Main SIR simulation engine (baseline scenario)
- `age_structured_discrete_SIR_model_no_school.py` - SIR model with school closure intervention
- `age_structured_discrete_SIR_model_no_work.py` - SIR model with workplace closure intervention
- `final_size_calculator.py` - Calculates theoretical final epidemic size using next-generation matrix
- `age_group_ranking_analysis.py` - Ranks countries by age-group-specific infection rates

### Analysis & Visualization

- `Fig2-chord-heatmap/` - Network structure visualization (chord diagrams and heatmaps)
  - `Chord diagram.py` - Generates chord diagrams showing inter-age-group connections
  - `Heatmap.py` - Creates heatmaps of contact matrices
  - `不同国家年龄组分布分析-new.py` - Age distribution analysis and visualization

- `fig3,fig4/` - Network degree distribution analysis
  - `degree_distribution_analysis.py` - Analyzes node degree distributions
  - `degree_distribution_loglog_analysis.py` - Log-log scale degree distribution plots

- `Fig5,Fig6/` - R0 and final size relationship analysis
  - `fig2,fig3.py` - Plots R0 vs final infection size with statistical annotations

- `Fig8/` - Age group comparison across countries
  - `Fig8.py` - Comparative analysis of age-specific infection rates

- `Fig9/` - Intervention impact on network structure
  - `Fig9.py` - Network metrics comparison between interventions
  - `age_distribution_analysis.py` - Cross-edge relative change analysis

- `Fig11/` - No-school intervention results
  - `Fig10.py` - Age group comparison under school closure scenario

- `Fig12/` - No-work intervention results
  - `Fig9.py` - Age group comparison under workplace closure scenario

### Data Directories

- `gexf_networks/` - Generated contact networks (baseline)
- `gexf_networks_no_school/` - Networks with school connections removed
- `gexf_networks_no_work/` - Networks with workplace connections removed
- `population fraction/` - Raw population distribution data (Excel files)
- `population_fraction_processed_csv/` - Processed population fractions (CSV)
- `processed_matrices/` - Symmetrized contact matrices (Pickle format)
- `results_by_country/` - Final size calculation results for all countries
- `Discrete_SIR_Analysis_Results*/` - SIR simulation outputs for different scenarios

